  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SDG 4 Coordination and Monitoring in Latin America and the Caribbean</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO Member States and Associate Members in Latin America and the Caribbean have established the Regional Coordination Mechanism, a technical and political dialogue platform designed to strengthen educational cooperation and support countries in advancing towards the achievement of SDG 4. Established in 2018, the mechanism is led by the Ministers of Education of the region, guided by the Regional Steering Committee for SDG 4, and supported by UNESCO Santiago in its role as Secretariat.

This project aims to support the preparation of the forthcoming Regional Meeting of Ministers of Education, the development of the Regional Steering Committee Workplan for 2026&#x2013;2027, and the monitoring of progress towards the achievement of the SDG 4 targets across the region.</narrative>
  </description>
